    "https://jobs.canterbury.ac.nz/jobdetails/ajid/mmgma/Senior-Business-Analyst,33414": {
      "title": "Senior Business Analyst",
      "description": "Senior Business Analyst -\n        University of Canterbury | Te Whare Wānanga o Waitaha Sign in Search jobs Search Show all jobs Keyword or Job Code Locations Any Work type Any Expertise Any show advanced Search Senior Business Analyst Te Ratonga Tautoko Hangarau | Digital Services Located in Ōtautahi | Christchurch, Aotearoa | New Zealand 5 weeks annual leave +5 days university holidays Professional development opportunities Permanent, 37.5 hours per week Generous employer contribution to superannuation (up to 6.75%) Āu Mahi | What You Will Do As our Senior Business Analyst, you will work closely with Product Managers, technical teams, and stakeholders across the University to translate business needs into well-defined solutions.  You will lead analysis activities across complex projects — from discovery and requirements gathering through to delivery — ensuring solutions are practical, aligned with strategy, and deliver real value. This role requires someone who can confidently move between strategic conversations with senior leaders and detailed technical discussions with development teams and you will be responsible for: Leading stakeholder engagement and requirements discovery across complex digital initiatives Analysing business processes, systems, and data to identify opportunities for improvement and innovation Translating business needs into clear requirements, process models, and solution designs Supporting Product Managers in developing achievable product roadmaps and delivery plans Guiding delivery teams during implementation, sprint planning, and deployment Facilitating workshops, large stakeholder meetings, and presentations Developing artefacts such as business cases, funding proposals, and change documentation Contributing to the development of data and integration practices aligned with University strategy Working closely with architects, developers, and project teams to ensure solutions are feasible and deliverable. This is an exciting opportunity to work across multiple initiatives, guiding the analysis and design of systems that enable better data, smarter integration, and improved business processes across the University. Mōu | Who You Are You are an experienced Senior Business Analyst who enjoys working across both technical and business domains. You bring strong analytical capability, excellent communication skills, and the ability to build trusted relationships with senior stakeholders.  To be successful in this role you will have: 10+ years’ experience as a Business Analyst within a complex IT or digital environment Strong experience in requirements gathering, gap analysis, data modelling, and process analysis Proven success delivering digital or software solutions Experience working with data and integration ecosystems Experience preparing business cases, procurement documentation, and funding artefacts Confidence facilitating large workshops and senior stakeholder discussions Familiarity with Agile and Lean delivery methodologies Exceptional communication, documentation, and organisational skills Hold a Bachelor’s degree in an IT-related discipline such as Computer Science or Software Engineering An alignment with our organisation's values and culture, promoting a positive and inclusive work environment. Mahi Ngātahi | Who You Will Work With Building world-class digital capability is crucial to the University of Canterbury's ongoing success. Digital Services is a large team, striving to provide a modern dynamic foundation from which the University (UC) can explore new business models and ways of working. Digital will transform how we work, behave, and the expectations of the communities we service. Ngā Painga o UC | Why UC At UC, being part of our team means more than just a job. We are committed to supporting our kaimahi | staff’s career and wellbeing with benefits designed to help our kaimahi grow and feel connected, supported and valued. UC’s Benefits approach is shaped by Ngā Uara | Our Values Whanaungatanga, Tiakitanga, and Manaakitanga. They are designed to be relevant, support and inspire our people, they include: 5 weeks annual leave +5 days university holidays generous employer contribution to superannuation (up to 6.75%) flexible working arrangements professional development opportunities supportive working environment a wide range of retail discounts across shopping, entertainment and travel on-campus staff discounts living in revitalised Ōtautahi | Christchurch, Aotearoa New Zealand a unique working environment in a beautiful campus with access to UC facilities such as UC RecCentre and Staff Club at discounted rates plus onsite cafés and eateries, and more. For more information, please visit us: https://www.canterbury.ac.nz/about-uc/work-at-uc/benefits-working-uc For more information about Te Whare Wānanga o Waitaha | University of Canterbury, please visit https://www.canterbury.ac.nz/ The closing date for this position is: 25 Septebmer 2026 (midnight, NZ time) Please note, applications will be reviewed as they are received, and interviews may take place before the close date. Pēhea te tono mai | How You Apply Applications for this position must be submitted via our careers website and should include a cover letter and resume. Please note, we do not accept applications by email, however we are happy to answer your queries in relation to the application process, please forward these to WorkatUC@canterbury.ac.nz You must have Aotearoa New Zealand or Australian citizenship/permanent residency to be considered for this role. Please note, this is an onsite position. Job Details Reference # 33414 Posted on 10 Sep 2026 Closes on 25 Sep 2026 23:55 Location(s) Christchurch Expertise Engineering, Information Technology Job level(s) Experienced Work type(s) Continuing (Permanent) full-time More details (document) PD_Senior Business Analyst.pdf Position description 1 Position description 2 Position description 3 Position description 4 Print Apply © University of Canterbury | Te Whare Wānanga o Waitaha Agency sign in Powered by SnapHire | Privacy policy 11 This site is powered by Snaphire (www.snaphire.com) This site uses Javascript and is required to search and apply for jobs. Your browser either doesn't support Javascript or it is disabled. If you are on a Corporate Network please contact your Administrator for further assistance. Loading . . ."
