    "https://jobs.canterbury.ac.nz/jobdetails/ajid/hJjna/Finance-Research-Administrator,33601": {
      "title": "Finance Research Administrator",
      "description": "Finance Research Administrator -\n        University of Canterbury | Te Whare Wānanga o Waitaha Sign in Search jobs Search Show all jobs Keyword or Job Code Locations Any Work type Any Expertise Any show advanced Search Finance Research Administrator Te Ratonga Ahumoni | Financial Services Located in Ōtautahi | Christchurch, Aotearoa | New Zealand 4 weeks annual leave +5 days university holidays Fixed term position until September 2027, 37.5 hours per week Generous employer contribution to superannuation (up to 6.75%) Kia hiwa rā, kia hiwa rā! He hiahia, he pūkenga nōu ki te mahi a te Finance Research Administrator? Nāia te pōwhiri nā Te Whare Wānanga o Waitaha kia tono mai i te tūranga nei. Āu Mahi | What You Will Do As Finance Research Administrator, you will work alongside the Post-award Team to support the financial administration of research and consultancy agreements. This includes invoicing, accounts receivable and payable processing, account reconciliations, managing credits, and following up on outstanding payments. The role also involves supporting the monitoring and reporting of research and consultancy income and expenditure, preparing financial information, coordinating grant closures and resolving financial matters with relevant colleagues and external stakeholders. Working closely with Financial Services and Research and Innovation, you will help deliver financial services seamlessly across the University. Mōu | Who You Are You are a finance professional who enjoys working with financial information, systems and processes with experience in contract administration and financial documentation. You will bring a proactive and collaborative approach to your work, along with the confidence to work independently when required. To be successful in this role, you will demonstrate: 3+ years’ experience working with database and finance systems, including invoicing and financial reporting. NCEA Level 3 or above qualification in accounting or finance. Advanced Microsoft Excel and strong data entry skills with proven experience using Oracle. Excellent attention to detail and a consistent focus on accuracy. Strong stakeholder relationship management skills, including the confidence to diplomatically follow up on outstanding payments while maintaining positive and professional relationships. An alignment with our organisation's values and culture, promoting a positive and inclusive work environment. Mahi Ngātahi | Who You Will Work With You will work collaboratively with teams across the University and external stakeholders to ensure the financial aspects of research and consultancy agreements are managed effectively and delivered in a timely manner. Ngā Painga o UC | Why UC At UC, being part of our team means more than just a job. We are committed to supporting our kaimahi | staff’s career and wellbeing with benefits designed to help our kaimahi grow and feel connected, supported and valued. 4 weeks annual leave +5 days university holidays generous employer contribution to superannuation (up to 6.75%) flexible working arrangement supportive working environment a wide range of retail discounts across shopping, entertainment and travel on-campus staff discounts living in revitalised Ōtautahi | Christchurch, Aotearoa New Zealand a unique working environment in a beautiful campus with access to UC facilities such as UC RecCentre and Staff Club at discounted rates plus onsite cafés and eateries, and more. We offer a range of benefits, for more information, please visit us: https://www.canterbury.ac.nz/about-uc/work-at-uc/benefits-working-uc . ( For more information about Te Whare Wānanga o Waitaha | University of Canterbury, please visit https://www.canterbury.ac.nz/ ) The closing date for this position is: 17 September 2026 (midnight, NZ time) Please note, applications will be reviewed as they are received, and interviews may take place before the close date. Pēhea te tono mai | How You Apply Applications for this position must be submitted via our careers website and should include a cover letter and resume. Please note, we do not accept applications by email, however we are happy to answer your queries in relation to the application process, please forward these to WorkatUC@canterbury.ac.nz You must have Aotearoa New Zealand or Australian citizenship/permanent residency or hold a valid NZ work visa to be considered for this role. Please note, this is an onsite position. Job Details Reference # 33601 Posted on 03 Sep 2026 Closes on 17 Sep 2026 23:55 Location(s) Christchurch Expertise Administration, Finance Job level(s) Experienced Work type(s) Fixed term full-time More details (document) PD_Finance Research Administrator.pdf Position description 1 Position description 2 Position description 3 Position description 4 Print Apply © University of Canterbury | Te Whare Wānanga o Waitaha Agency sign in Powered by SnapHire | Privacy policy 11 This site is powered by Snaphire (www.snaphire.com) This site uses Javascript and is required to search and apply for jobs. Your browser either doesn't support Javascript or it is disabled. If you are on a Corporate Network please contact your Administrator for further assistance. Loading . . ."
